    "created_at": "2026-01-22T07:59:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-22T07:59:45Z",
    "body": "When writing this algorithm in JavaScript (https://github.com/jsdom/whatwg-mimetype/blob/main/lib/sniff.js) the meaning of this step was pretty clear. `supplied-type` can end up being either a MIME type record, or null, because step 1 sets it to null and it's possible nothing sets it to a non-null value in steps 2-4. So the step 5 check could equivalently be written `if (suppliedType === null) { return undefined; }`.\n\nThis is basically a kind of silly conversion between null and undefined which I have [omitted](https://github.com/jsdom/whatwg-mimetype/blob/76b29fb2635157c72a68bf9fa44d32b890bc655c/lib/sniff.js#L671-L673) in my implementation.\n\nSee also https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/81 and my comment there.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
